postcolonialism, an area of studies whose principal home has been in litera-
ture departments? I attempt to answer this question by discussing how, and
in what sense, Subaltern Studies could be seen as a postcolonial project of
writing history. It should be clariﬁed, however, that my concentration here
on the relationship between postcolonialism and historiography overlooks
the contributions that other disciplines—political science, legal studies, an-
